WEBVTT

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:18.250
<i>How about it? Let's kick
Team Mizonokuchi's ass together!</i>

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.450
<i>But even so...</i>

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:26.220
<i>I totally don't feel up for it.</i>

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:28.590
I thought you would be here, you jerk!

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.260
You sure are
one hell of an easy guy to find.

00:00:33.330 --> 00:00:35.500
Makoto Ono?

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:44.770
ORIGINAL WORK BY RENSUKE OSHIKIRI

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:14.200
<i>THE ZUNZUN CULT PLOT</i>

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:18.670
<i>THE ZUNZUN CULT PLOT</i>

00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:21.100
How... How come you're here?

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:23.970
Your friends back home told me,

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:26.880
"Haruo is turning into a Shibuya hoodlum."

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.010
<i>Darn that Miyao.</i>

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:34.650
I never thought you had the balls
to become a hoodlum!

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.020
I'm not!

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:40.660
And after I bought you <i>Tokimeki Memorial</i>
to turn you into a romantic guy,

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:44.390
you turn into a delinquent just before
your second year in high school.

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:47.930
It's biased to think I would become
a delinquent just by being in Shibuya.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:49.700
-And?
-What?

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:51.530
How are things with you and Akira lately?

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:53.870
Have you been meeting at the arcade?

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.310
No. I haven't seen her
since she came to my place the other day.

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:59.570
What the hell is your problem?

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:02.510
I mean, I've been looking
to see if she's there,

00:03:02.580 --> 00:03:04.310
but it seems she hasn't come at all.

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:05.850
That's not true.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.620
<i>Apparently, she's gotten lots of practice
at that new one, </i>Street Fighter Alpha 2.

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:15.260
<i>You know that dude
with the hairy chest? Zanda? Zan...</i>

00:03:15.320 --> 00:03:16.590
<i>-Zangief.
-Yes, him.</i>

00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:19.060
<i>She's pretty happy that he's included.</i>

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:22.730
<i>Apparently, Moemi has given her
more leeway lately,</i>

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:26.100
<i>so she's been going to
the arcade sometimes.</i>

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.470
Is that right?

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:31.270
Then I guess I kept on just missing her.

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:36.880
The more you hang out in Shibuya,
the less you'll be able to see Akira.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:40.880
I'm sure she's missing you terribly,
that girl.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:46.490
<i>I see. Ono has been getting practice
at </i>Street Fighter Alpha 2<i>, has she?</i>

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:50.390
<i>If I keep wasting time like this,
she'll get way ahead of me.</i>

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:55.360
<i>Unless I can become overwhelmingly
good at it before I fight her,</i>

00:03:56.330 --> 00:03:59.330
<i>I'll be permanently eating her dust.</i>

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:04.340
<i>I wish I could fight against Ono.</i>

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:10.380
It's named <i>Street Fighter Alpha 2</i>,
but when the heck is three coming out?

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:11.710
Don't ask that.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:15.280
It's like they're making progress
but not getting anywhere.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:18.190
That sounds exactly like the relationship
between you and Akira.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:21.920
-That's so dumb.
-That is not dumb!

00:04:21.990 --> 00:04:24.160
You're coming back home right now!

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:28.630
Haruo! Perfect timing!

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:32.100
We were going to ask you
to join us for some karaoke.

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:33.500
Is that your sister, Haruo?

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:36.940
Come on, you! Sing!

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:39.910
Aren't you going to fucking sing?

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:43.280
-I said, why the fuck aren't you singing?
-Wait, lady!

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:44.810
Wait! No!

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.820
Your clothes are soaking!

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:55.290
We're just going to have to
get you changed, miss.

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:03.800
Pretty damn good, wouldn't you say?

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:06.300
-Totally hot!
-Damn nice!

00:05:06.370 --> 00:05:09.270
What do you think, my little brother?
Cute, right?

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:10.970
I guess it's okay.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.510
Okay! Time to go to Tower Records!

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:17.310
-We've got to practice for the match...
-Everyone, follow me!

00:05:17.380 --> 00:05:18.780
-Okay!
-Okay!

00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:27.990
<i>I wanted to practice
</i>Street Fighter Alpha 2.

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:31.660
<i>Haruo, Shibuya isn't the place for you.</i>

00:05:33.290 --> 00:05:37.270
<i>It's time for you to return home.
You have family there.</i>

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:41.900
<i>You're right.
I'm sure Mom is worried about me too.</i>

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:44.610
<i>I'll take Makoto with me
back to my own territory.</i>

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:46.810
<i>-I'm sure Ono is...
-Haruo?</i>

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:48.440
<i>Haruo!</i>

00:05:53.650 --> 00:05:55.920
Mrs. Yaguchi!

00:05:56.380 --> 00:05:57.820
Mrs. Yaguchi!

00:05:57.890 --> 00:06:00.120
Well, if it isn't Ziiya.

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:03.520
Are you back to being Akira's chauffeur?

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:08.860
Yes. Thanks to your help, Ms. Moemi has
allowed me back into this position.

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:12.630
But I had to promise to give up
my beloved pachinko!

00:06:18.770 --> 00:06:23.110
I couldn't care less about fashion,
but I really liked that one!

00:06:23.180 --> 00:06:26.350
I can't believe Moemi
ripped it off me and burned it!

00:06:26.880 --> 00:06:30.120
How dare you wear
something so unbecoming as that!

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:35.090
I never knew Shibuya was
such a fascinating place.

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:38.790
I kind of understand why
Haruo hangs out there.

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:42.800
Haruo said he was ostracized
here in his hometown.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:46.500
I think he was just trying to escape
and ended up in Shibuya.

00:06:47.070 --> 00:06:51.710
He had been going to the arcade,
but the idiot kept on just missing you.

00:06:51.770 --> 00:06:53.270
He said he looked all over for you.

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:55.780
He wants to fight you
in <i>Street Fighter Alpha 2</i>.

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:57.410
He's dying to see you...

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:00.250
I guess you wouldn't believe that lie.

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:02.250
But don't you worry, Akira.

00:07:02.480 --> 00:07:05.950
I swear I'll bring that guy back.

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:10.430
He said something about
a team match tonight in Shibuya,

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:12.390
so while Moemi isn't looking...

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:26.810
<i>It's the Fighting Vipers East-West Battle!</i>

00:07:27.380 --> 00:07:29.280
In the east,
the ten members of Team Shibuya.

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:32.010
In the west, the ten members
of Team Mizonokuchi.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:35.550
This single-elimination match
will determine the victor,

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:37.420
Team Shibuya or Team Mizonokuchi!

00:07:37.720 --> 00:07:43.060
If Team Mizonokuchi wins,
Shibuya Kaikan is ours!

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:45.130
Just you try and win!

00:07:51.130 --> 00:07:52.530
What's with that outfit?

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:57.640
Hidaka... I didn't have a choice.

00:07:57.770 --> 00:08:01.810
If I wore my usual clothes,
they would all say I look lame.

00:08:01.880 --> 00:08:05.280
I think you look best
in your ordinary clothes, Yaguchi.

00:08:06.110 --> 00:08:09.080
Yaguchi! I'm totally rooting for you!

00:08:09.150 --> 00:08:12.250
Kick the tails of those dumb
Mizonokuchi people.

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:15.520
What's wrong with you, Mayumayu? Hey!

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:18.730
Don't let those country bumpkins
from Kanagawa get the best of you.

00:08:18.790 --> 00:08:22.500
I think it's so stupid to get
all worked up over silly games.

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:24.800
Oh, my god!

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:28.300
Those Mizonokuchi people are
way more frightening than Shibuya punks.

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:30.870
Koharu, calm down.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:33.710
-If you let the opponent provoke...
-Nikotama!

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:36.340
Please let me play first!

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:39.450
-But...
-Please!

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.260
Get him, Hidaka!

00:08:48.220 --> 00:08:49.560
That was awesome, Hidaka!

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:51.830
That's five guys down!

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:54.260
When did you get so good?

00:08:55.500 --> 00:09:00.270
<i>Koharu, you're not winning by skill.
It's your anger that set you on fire.</i>

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:14.680
Damn, Hidaka! You could go the whole way!

00:09:16.520 --> 00:09:18.790
Goddamn Team Mizonokuchi!

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:21.890
They've unleashed
their most brutal gamer on us!

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:26.130
<i>Who gives a damn about a full-out war
between Team Mizonokuchi and Team Shibuya?</i>

00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:31.300
Somebody stop that fucking bitch!

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:33.100
<i>This stupid thing...</i>

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:35.800
<i>I alone...</i>

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:39.140
<i>will put to an end!</i>

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:48.550
<i>I can't believe Hidaka.</i>

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:51.820
<i>She's putting on such a show.</i>

00:10:02.300 --> 00:10:03.930
-Just one more!
-Just one more!

00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:05.900
-Just one more!
-Just one more!

00:10:06.470 --> 00:10:07.970
-Just one more!
-Just one more!

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:10.270
<i>Nobody can even touch Koharu.</i>

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:11.570
-Just one more!
-Just one more!

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:14.610
<i>And now it comes down
to this battle again.</i>

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:16.840
You can do it, Yaguchi!

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:19.150
If you win everything,
I'll give you a nice treat.

00:10:19.210 --> 00:10:20.450
What?

00:10:23.420 --> 00:10:24.690
You're our last chance!

00:10:24.750 --> 00:10:27.120
We're counting on you, boss!

00:10:28.490 --> 00:10:29.960
You can do it, Hidaka!

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:32.790
This will make ten straight wins!

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:49.710
Haruo!

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:54.580
<i>This is bad. I'm clearly not
as proficient as Hidaka is.</i>

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:00.090
Say, Mayumayu,

00:11:00.620 --> 00:11:04.030
you wouldn't happen to have
your eyes set on Yaguchi, would you?

00:11:04.090 --> 00:11:06.560
Yes. I mean, he's so sweet and naive.

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.800
A simple guy like that,

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:12.530
I'll get him in the sack
and ride him good!

00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:15.170
<i>If you think you can get him in the sack,</i>

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:17.970
<i>then I can certainly do the same!</i>

00:11:20.140 --> 00:11:23.310
KOHARU HIDAKA
10 CONSECUTIVE WINS

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:25.610
Damn, that was good, Hidaka!

00:11:25.680 --> 00:11:28.950
That's so cool how you won it all
by blowing off his armor!

00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:31.550
Mizonokuchi skunked them!

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:37.930
Hey, keep your paws off my boyfriend.

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:45.370
That was so stupid.

00:11:46.700 --> 00:11:48.100
Don't you think it's stupid

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:51.710
to battle between cliques
or over turf with video games?

00:11:52.310 --> 00:11:56.140
But isn't it way more sensible
than fighting with fists?

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:59.450
It may not seem like
they understand one another,

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:03.650
but they inevitably see eye-to-eye
when battling through the video screen.

00:12:04.420 --> 00:12:06.850
I don't think you can call that a fight.

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:10.360
You know, that's pretty deep.

00:12:10.730 --> 00:12:11.830
That may be so,

00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:15.100
but your ten-in-a-row blowout
was terrifying!

00:12:15.160 --> 00:12:19.030
It's going to take a while to get over
that final humiliating defeat.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:21.600
-I'm sorry.
-Don't apologize!

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:23.340
That makes me even more miserable!

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:25.010
-That's not what I mean.
-What?

00:12:25.070 --> 00:12:27.240
It's for saying that you're my boyfriend.

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:31.680
I know you said that because
Mayumayu was being a nauseating flirt.

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:33.510
You don't need to apologize for that.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:36.820
The other day,
I said you were annoying and stuff.

00:12:37.490 --> 00:12:38.950
I was just kidding, you know.

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:41.860
It's all right.
It's water under the bridge.

00:12:41.920 --> 00:12:43.890
Then go on a date with me now.

00:12:43.960 --> 00:12:45.960
What's the reasoning behind that?

00:12:46.590 --> 00:12:48.930
I defeated you earlier.

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:51.970
-Are you serious?
-Okay, you don't have to call it a date.

00:12:52.600 --> 00:12:55.900
Let's just say we're out for some fun.
That'll be fine, right?

00:12:55.970 --> 00:12:58.140
Yes, I guess that's fine.

00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:02.580
But where will we go in this rain?

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:06.380
How about some other arcade?

00:13:07.580 --> 00:13:09.850
You sure you don't have to
tell those other guys?

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:12.850
It's just fine.

00:13:17.160 --> 00:13:21.400
Darn that Hidaka chick! Who would have
thought she was Yaguchi's girlfriend?

00:13:21.460 --> 00:13:24.500
Seriously?
Haruo has a girlfriend that cute?

00:13:27.200 --> 00:13:28.440
This really ticks me off!

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:31.470
They both quietly snuck away!

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:36.280
And I was all set on
taking Yaguchi's virginity too!

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:40.080
I bet they're making out
somewhere right now.

00:13:42.920 --> 00:13:43.750
<i>It's the General.</i>

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:54.760
-What? What is it?
-What's going on?

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:59.000
That girl defeated the General!

00:13:59.470 --> 00:14:01.370
And she did it with Marco!

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:04.070
You must be kidding!

00:14:04.140 --> 00:14:05.570
DIAGNOSIS: MORTALLY WOUNDED

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:17.480
SHIBUYA STATION

00:14:17.550 --> 00:14:20.960
ATTENTION: PASSENGERS

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:26.930
There was a lightning strike in Nikotama.

00:14:26.990 --> 00:14:31.170
They don't know when the Den-en-toshi
or Oimachi Lines will be running again.

00:14:31.230 --> 00:14:33.130
What a pain.

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:37.400
Oh, well. It'll cost a ton, but I guess
we had better take a taxi home.

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:41.410
What a waste! What's wrong with
staying here until morning?

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:43.080
Staying here until morning?

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:45.710
What are we supposed to do until morning?

00:14:46.850 --> 00:14:48.920
Whatever we do, we'll need money.

00:14:48.980 --> 00:14:51.490
We're still better off taking a taxi home.

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:53.920
I bet your parents are
worried about you too.

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:56.560
Here. Use this to call home.

00:14:58.860 --> 00:14:59.790
What's the matter?

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:04.230
<i>No! If I call home,
they'll come in the car to pick me up.</i>

00:15:04.770 --> 00:15:06.970
-What's wrong, Hidaka?
-I'm hungry!

00:15:07.570 --> 00:15:09.000
I'm hungry.

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:12.510
There's no point in waiting here
for the trains to start running.

00:15:12.570 --> 00:15:14.480
Why don't we get something to eat?

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:16.410
Come to think of it, I'm starving.

00:15:16.480 --> 00:15:19.380
We can call my parents after that. Okay?

00:15:19.450 --> 00:15:22.720
I guess you're right.
Let's have a late dinner.

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:32.990
Darn that Hidaka chick! Who would have
thought she was Yaguchi's girlfriend?

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:34.830
Get over it, would you?

00:15:34.900 --> 00:15:37.630
That ticks me off!
That totally ticks me off!

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:40.000
They both quietly snuck away too!

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:17.270
Hey.

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:23.640
How can you burst out laughing
right in my face?

00:16:24.110 --> 00:16:25.680
Dang, you're rude!

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:30.720
-I wonder why.
-What?

00:16:30.780 --> 00:16:34.660
How come such a plain guy like you is
so darn popular?

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:36.720
What's your problem?

00:16:36.790 --> 00:16:40.290
How can you keep insulting me to my face?

00:16:40.690 --> 00:16:43.800
Well, I would agree
that I'm pretty darn plain.

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:49.400
You should have more self-confidence.
You're pretty sweet, Yaguchi.

00:16:49.470 --> 00:16:51.370
You're making fun of me. I know it!

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:54.840
Yes, I'm making fun of you a little.

00:16:59.310 --> 00:17:00.310
What? What is it?

00:17:02.920 --> 00:17:05.220
You really are mysterious, Yaguchi.

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:08.460
How come it's so much fun being with you?

00:17:09.460 --> 00:17:12.390
Isn't it the video games
we play together that are fun?

00:17:13.390 --> 00:17:14.860
It's not just the games.

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:17.130
It's because of you, Yaguchi.

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:22.240
Hey, have you played <i>Marvel Super Heroes</i>?
That one's awesome, isn't it?

00:17:23.540 --> 00:17:26.310
If you invite me to play, Yaguchi,
I'll play it.

00:17:27.410 --> 00:17:29.680
What game have you been
playing lately, Hidaka?

00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:31.680
I heard you've played quite a few.

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:37.180
<i>Soul Edge.</i>

00:17:38.090 --> 00:17:39.590
<i>Soul Edge</i>...

00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:43.820
Yaguchi, you know, recently,

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:47.030
no matter what I do,
I feel oddly frustrated.

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:51.100
I thought about why that is.

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:53.530
And, it's you, Yaguchi.

00:17:54.000 --> 00:17:55.170
<i>What is she talking about?</i>

00:17:56.600 --> 00:17:59.410
I want to tease you really badly

00:18:00.240 --> 00:18:01.510
and slap you

00:18:01.980 --> 00:18:03.480
and kick you.

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:05.680
You've been playing
too many fighting games.

00:18:05.750 --> 00:18:07.210
You should play more chill--

00:18:07.310 --> 00:18:08.950
But it's not because I hate you.

00:18:10.050 --> 00:18:11.090
It's the opposite.

00:18:12.720 --> 00:18:18.130
Whenever I see you, I can't keep myself
from giving in to these odd impulses.

00:18:21.900 --> 00:18:25.970
Lately, I keep having dreams
about being hugged by you.

00:18:27.330 --> 00:18:29.070
What does "hug" mean again?

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:31.070
Holding someone tightly in your arms.

00:18:33.110 --> 00:18:36.280
I have dreams
with you in them too, Hidaka.

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:40.550
You attack me with Sieger and stuff.
They're usually nightmares.

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:42.950
It felt so nice...

00:18:44.380 --> 00:18:46.490
being held tight by you in my dreams.

00:18:47.790 --> 00:18:49.990
You sure have a dirty mind, Hidaka.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:52.460
Yes, I have a dirty mind. So what?

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:54.190
Don't say that.

00:19:00.730 --> 00:19:03.440
We're first-year students
in high school, you know.

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:06.840
Isn't it only natural for us
to think about these things?

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:10.840
It sure was nice.

00:19:10.910 --> 00:19:12.810
I want to have that dream again.

00:19:13.350 --> 00:19:15.780
Why don't we talk about
<i>Street Fighter Alpha 2</i> instead?

00:19:15.850 --> 00:19:19.020
No. Don't use games to change the subject.

00:19:23.990 --> 00:19:25.990
I'm pretty tired now.

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:31.300
Well, that only makes sense.
Especially after winning ten in a row.

00:19:32.470 --> 00:19:35.170
I want to go somewhere with a bed. Can we?

00:19:35.540 --> 00:19:39.270
-You mean, me and you together?
-That's right.

00:19:40.440 --> 00:19:43.280
A place where men and women go.
Know what I mean?

00:19:44.110 --> 00:19:47.810
I know at least that much.
There are a bunch in Dogenzaka.

00:19:47.880 --> 00:19:49.050
Have you been to one?

00:19:49.580 --> 00:19:50.850
Of course, I haven't!

00:19:51.420 --> 00:19:52.550
We have to go.

00:19:53.190 --> 00:19:55.820
We have to go to one together.

00:19:58.190 --> 00:20:00.330
Please, Yaguchi!

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:33.190
Hidaka?

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:37.900
Hey!

00:20:58.020 --> 00:20:59.050
Just dreaming it...

00:21:01.890 --> 00:21:03.120
isn't good enough!

00:21:05.290 --> 00:21:08.300
Yaguchi, you really are mean!

00:21:09.760 --> 00:21:13.170
How can you put a woman through
such embarrassment? Damn you!

00:21:14.570 --> 00:21:16.800
You'll never have any idea
what it feels like

00:21:17.700 --> 00:21:20.470
to put your feelings
on the line like I have!

00:21:21.140 --> 00:21:24.850
You're always acting so cool!
I can't stand that about you!

00:21:24.910 --> 00:21:30.050
Hidaka! Only adults who want to make love
go to places like that!

00:21:30.280 --> 00:21:32.820
I was tired,
so I just wanted to sleep there!

00:21:33.290 --> 00:21:35.560
I never would have attacked you!

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:37.220
What? What did you say?

00:21:38.430 --> 00:21:39.530
Is that right?

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:42.230
No! I would have jumped all over you!

00:21:43.560 --> 00:21:46.200
Yaguchi! Please! Hold me tight!

00:21:46.800 --> 00:21:48.570
I'll never ask you again! Please!

00:21:51.510 --> 00:21:52.940
Please!

00:23:37.840 --> 00:23:42.020
<i>When you play a game that you used to be
addicted to but haven't played in a while,</i>

00:23:42.480 --> 00:23:45.390
<i>doesn't it bring back memories
as you play?</i>

00:23:45.750 --> 00:23:48.590
<i>The bosses you couldn't defeat.
The final level you couldn't clear.</i>
